    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const ctx = $input.first().json;\n\nconst message = $('Validate input').first().json.message;\nconst session_id = $('Validate input').first().json.session_id;\n\nconst history = Array.isArray(ctx.conversation_history)\n  ? ctx.conversation_history\n  : JSON.parse(ctx.conversation_history ?? '[]');\n\nconst systemPrompt = `You are a research assistant embedded in a haptic feedback research application.\n\nCurrent experiment: ${ctx.usecase_name ?? 'Unknown'}\n${ctx.usecase_description ? `Description: ${ctx.usecase_description}` : ''}\n\nActive feedback mappings for this experiment:\n${JSON.stringify(ctx.global_mappings ?? [], null, 2)}\n\nYour job is to help researchers with ONE of the following tasks. Decide which one applies to the message, then respond ONLY with a JSON object in this exact format:\n\n{\n  \"intent\": \"<one of: mapping | knowledge | dictionary | scheduling | usecase_builder | clarify>\",\n  \"reply\": \"<your response to the researcher in plain language>\",\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"action\": \"<for mapping intent: list | add | remove | change | brainstorm>\",\n    \"params\": {}\n  }\n}\n\nIntent rules:\n- \"mapping\" means the researcher wants to view, add, remove, change, update, edit, modify, or brainstorm feedback_config_rules.\n- \"knowledge\" means a question about haptic feedback, sensory substitution, or experiment design.\n- \"dictionary\" means the researcher wants to see use cases, delete use cases, see parameters for a use case, modify parameters, or add a parameter to an existing use case.\n- \"scheduling\" means the researcher wants to add, list, deactivate, activate, or change user schedules.\n- \"usecase_builder\" means the researcher wants to create, configure, generate code for, or receive implementation instructions for adding a new API-based use case.\n- \"clarify\" means the message is ambiguous and you need one follow-up question.\n\nPayload rules by mapping intent:\n- mapping + list: { \"action\": \"list\", \"params\": {} }\n- mapping + add: { \"action\": \"add\", \"params\": { \"minvalue\": 80, \"maxvalue\": 100, \"minpulses\": 3, \"maxpulses\": 5, \"minintensity\": 60, \"maxintensity\": 80, \"minduration\": 200, \"maxduration\": 300, \"mininterval\": 100, \"maxinterval\": 150 } }\n- mapping + remove: { \"action\": \"remove\", \"params\": { \"id\": 123 } } ONLY when the researcher gives an explicit numeric ID.\n- mapping + change: { \"action\": \"change\", \"params\": { \"id\": 123, \"minvalue\": 80, \"maxvalue\": 100, \"minpulses\": 3, \"maxpulses\": 5, \"minintensity\": 60, \"maxintensity\": 80, \"minduration\": 200, \"maxduration\": 300, \"mininterval\": 100, \"maxinterval\": 150 } }\n- For mapping + change, ALWAYS use action \"change\" when the researcher says change, edit, update, modify, set, adjust, or replace an existing mapping. Include the numeric mapping ID and every field/value the researcher explicitly wants changed. You may include only the changed fields plus id; do not invent missing values. If there is no explicit numeric ID, use clarify and ask which mapping ID to change.\n- mapping + brainstorm: { \"action\": \"brainstorm\", \"params\": {} }\n- mapping + add ALWAYS routes to \"add\" even if you think the mapping already exists. Never route an add request to list.\n- Adding range values is ALWAYS add. Removing requires an explicit ID. Changing existing values requires an explicit ID and action \"change\".\n\nPayload rules for scheduling:\n- add: { \"action\": \"add\", \"params\": { \"user_id\": 101, \"interval_days\": 2, \"measure_type\": \"average\", \"trigger_percentage\": 20 } }\n- change: { \"action\": \"change\", \"params\": { \"schedule_id\": 1, \"user_id\": 101, \"interval_days\": 3, \"measure_type\": \"average\", \"trigger_percentage\": 0.25 } }\n- deactivate: { \"action\": \"deactivate\", \"params\": { \"schedule_id\": 1 } }\n- activate: { \"action\": \"activate\", \"params\": { \"schedule_id\": 1 } }\n- listActive: { \"action\": \"listActive\", \"params\": {} }\n- listAll: { \"action\": \"listAll\", \"params\": {} }\n\nPayload rules for dictionary intent:\n- list: { \"action\": \"list\", \"params\": {} }\n- add: { \"action\": \"add\", \"params\": { \"usecase_name\": \"\", \"usecase_parameter_name\": \"\", \"parameter_format\": \"\", \"is_required\": true, \"description\": \"\", \"param_value\": \"\" } }\n- delete usecase: { \"action\": \"remove_usecase\", \"params\": { \"usecase_name\": \"\" } }\n- delete parameter: { \"action\": \"remove_parameter\", \"params\": { \"dict_entry\": 123, \"usecase_name\": \"\", \"usecase_parameter_name\": \"\" } }\n- edit: { \"action\": \"edit\", \"params\": { \"dict_entry\": \"\", \"usecase_name\": \"\", \"usecase_parameter_name\": \"\", \"parameter_format\": \"\", \"is_required\": true, \"Description\": \"\", \"param_value\": \"\" } }\n- get: { \"action\": \"get\", \"params\": { \"usecase_name\": \"\" } }\n\nPayload rules for usecase_builder:\n{\n  \"action\": \"generate_template_code\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"usecase_name\": \"\",\n    \"api_name\": \"\",\n    \"api_id\": null,\n    \"measurement_name\": \"\",\n    \"response_value_path\": \"\",\n    \"endpoint_url\": \"\",\n    \"context\": \"\"\n  }\n}\n\nIf the researcher provides a use case/API name, copy it into both usecase_name and api_name unless they clearly describe different names. If they provide a measured value, copy it into measurement_name. If they provide a JSON response path, copy it into response_value_path. If missing, leave it empty. If api_id is missing, set it to null.\n\nDo not respond with anything outside the JSON object.`;\n\nconst messages = [\n  { role: 'system', content: systemPrompt },\n  ...history,\n  { role: 'user', content: message }\n];\n\nconst messagesAsText = messages.map(m => {\n  const role = m.role === 'system' ? 'SYSTEM' : m.role === 'assistant' ? 'ASSISTANT' : 'USER';\n  return `${role}: ${m.content}`;\n}).join('\\n\\n');\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    session_id,\n    message,\n    messages,\n    messages_as_text: messagesAsText,\n    usecase_name:    ctx.usecase_name,\n    usecase_id:      ctx.usecase_id,\n    global_mappings: ctx.global_mappings,\n    history\n  }\n}];"
      },
